	<string name="ordenar_teclado_titulo">Choose the braille keyboard menu</string>
	<string name="ordenar_teclado_res">What one finger up shows on the braille keyboard, and in which order</string>
	<string name="ordenar_teclado_explicacion">The checked options appear in the braille keyboard menu (one finger up), in this order. Uncheck the ones you do not want. Mention suggestions and remove calibration only appear when they make sense. To change the order of one, use Move up and Move down in its actions menu (or long press it).</string>
	<string name="ordenar_lector_teclado_titulo">Choose the screen reader menu on the braille keyboard</string>
	<string name="ordenar_lector_teclado_res">Tiresias actions at hand while you type, with three fingers up: the curtain, the time, the voice, the music…</string>
	<string name="ordenar_lector_teclado_explicacion">The checked options appear in the screen reader menu of the braille keyboard (three fingers up), in this order. Only the Tiresias actions that work while you type are here: those that say something or change a setting, never those that open a window or move around the screen. Any of them can also be put directly on a keyboard gesture, in «Braille keyboard gestures».</string>
